00:00.000 --> 00:05.680
So welcome everyone. I want to talk today about occupancy grid maps which is a

00:05.680 --> 00:09.960
representation of the environment that a lot of mobile robots use. So they use

00:09.960 --> 00:14.160
these types of map in order to represent the space around them and in order to do

00:14.160 --> 00:18.580
various of different tasks such as planning a path towards a goal location.

00:18.580 --> 00:23.440
And these occupancy grid maps can be seen as kind of architectural floor

00:23.440 --> 00:29.200
plans. So what they do, they basically store information about which parts of

00:29.240 --> 00:32.200
